1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:18,180
What's today's video about? It's conversations at beauty salons and barbershops. Be careful what you say! There’ll be a Japanese question hidden somewhere in the video—leave a comment if you catch it!

2
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:19,680
Scene 1: Let’s Talk About Bento!

3
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:23,214
What are we talking about today?

4
00:00:23,237 --> 00:00:25,603
Bento!

5
00:00:25,626 --> 00:00:29,269
Bento? That’s great!

6
00:00:29,293 --> 00:00:33,666
I love bento!

7
00:00:33,690 --> 00:00:38,490
Do you eat bento every day?

8
00:00:38,513 --> 00:00:43,788
Yeah, I eat bento every day.

9
00:00:43,811 --> 00:00:46,544
I made one this morning.

10
00:00:46,567 --> 00:00:50,626
Do you make it yourself every day?

11
00:00:50,650 --> 00:00:52,860
Wow, that’s impressive!

12
00:00:52,883 --> 00:00:56,974
Yep, I make it myself.

13
00:00:56,998 --> 00:00:59,565
It’s just simple cooking.

14
00:00:59,588 --> 00:01:03,831
What’s in today’s bento?

15
00:01:03,854 --> 00:01:06,672
There’s white rice.

16
00:01:06,696 --> 00:01:11,329
And a red pickled plum on top of the rice.

17
00:01:11,352 --> 00:01:13,319
That looks so pretty!

18
00:01:13,342 --> 00:01:16,575
What else is in there?

19
00:01:16,598 --> 00:01:19,665
There’s yellow tamagoyaki (Japanese omelet).

20
00:01:19,688 --> 00:01:23,754
And some brown meat too.

21
00:01:23,777 --> 00:01:27,377
Whoa, that’s a lot!

22
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:29,667
Looks amazing!

23
00:01:29,690 --> 00:01:33,857
Yeah, it’s really delicious.

24
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:36,716
There are green veggies too!

25
00:01:36,739 --> 00:01:38,943
That’s wonderful!

26
00:01:38,967 --> 00:01:43,623
The bento has so many colors!

27
00:01:43,646 --> 00:01:45,325
That’s right.

28
00:01:45,349 --> 00:01:49,682
That’s why bento looks so beautiful.

29
00:01:49,705 --> 00:01:53,484
I don’t have a bento today.

30
00:01:53,507 --> 00:01:56,107
That’s too bad.

31
00:01:56,130 --> 00:01:57,965
I see.

32
00:01:57,989 --> 00:02:01,641
What are you having for lunch today?

33
00:02:01,665 --> 00:02:05,131
I went to the convenience store today.

34
00:02:05,154 --> 00:02:09,754
I bought bread and juice there.

35
00:02:09,777 --> 00:02:12,744
Convenience store bread is tasty too, right?

36
00:02:12,767 --> 00:02:15,249
I like it.

37
00:02:15,272 --> 00:02:18,239
Yeah, it’s good.

38
00:02:18,262 --> 00:02:22,917
But I eat convenience store bread every day.

39
00:02:22,940 --> 00:02:25,786
Eating it every day isn’t great, though.

40
00:02:25,809 --> 00:02:29,142
Bento is healthier for you.

41
00:02:29,165 --> 00:02:32,165
And it doesn’t cost much either.

42
00:02:32,188 --> 00:02:34,080
That’s true.

43
00:02:34,104 --> 00:02:38,371
Homemade bento is really cheap.

44
00:02:38,394 --> 00:02:43,594
Yeah, that’s why I make it every day.

45
00:02:43,617 --> 00:02:45,905
It’s fun too!

46
00:02:45,929 --> 00:02:48,575
Is cooking hard?

47
00:02:48,599 --> 00:02:52,447
I’m not good at cooking.

48
00:02:52,470 --> 00:02:55,643
No, it’s not hard at all!

49
00:02:55,666 --> 00:02:59,070
Let’s start with simple dishes.

50
00:02:59,094 --> 00:03:01,660
What kind of dish would you like to try?

51
00:03:01,683 --> 00:03:04,973
For example, let's talk about onigiri.

52
00:03:04,997 --> 00:03:08,463
Onigiri is really simple to make.

53
00:03:08,486 --> 00:03:10,530
Onigiri, you say?

54
00:03:10,554 --> 00:03:12,487
Sounds good!

55
00:03:12,510 --> 00:03:16,316
Do you like onigiri?

56
00:03:16,339 --> 00:03:19,711
Yes, I love it!

57
00:03:19,735 --> 00:03:23,068
Alright, let’s talk about onigiri.

58
00:03:23,091 --> 00:03:25,058
Sounds good!

59
00:03:25,081 --> 00:03:32,186
You can find the link to review today’s video in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without prior notice.

60
00:03:32,186 --> 00:03:33,686
Scene 2: Let’s Talk About Onigiri Preferences

61
00:03:33,686 --> 00:03:38,652
Now, let’s talk about onigiri.

62
00:03:38,675 --> 00:03:40,642
Sounds good!

63
00:03:40,665 --> 00:03:43,522
Let’s get right into it!

64
00:03:43,545 --> 00:03:47,032
Onigiri is just so delicious.

65
00:03:47,056 --> 00:03:51,333
What kind of onigiri do you like?

66
00:03:51,356 --> 00:03:55,368
I love salmon onigiri.

67
00:03:55,391 --> 00:03:59,161
What kind of onigiri do you like?

68
00:03:59,185 --> 00:04:03,645
I prefer umeboshi (pickled plum) onigiri.

69
00:04:03,668 --> 00:04:08,241
It’s a little sour, but so tasty!

70
00:04:08,265 --> 00:04:11,831
Umeboshi is great.

71
00:04:11,854 --> 00:04:16,021
The red color is so pretty.

72
00:04:16,044 --> 00:04:17,452
That’s true.

73
00:04:17,476 --> 00:04:21,309
Having something red in your bento box is always nice.

74
00:04:21,332 --> 00:04:25,099
That makes me really happy.

75
00:04:25,122 --> 00:04:30,372
Sometimes, I also buy tuna mayo onigiri.

76
00:04:30,395 --> 00:04:33,970
You can find it in convenience stores all the time.

77
00:04:33,993 --> 00:04:37,127
Tuna mayo is delicious too.

78
00:04:37,150 --> 00:04:41,083
It’s really popular with younger people.

79
00:04:41,106 --> 00:04:46,039
Do you wrap the nori around it before eating?

80
00:04:46,062 --> 00:04:47,596
Yes, I do.

81
00:04:47,619 --> 00:04:51,185
I wrap it right before eating.

82
00:04:51,208 --> 00:04:55,460
I love the crispy texture of the nori.

83
00:04:55,484 --> 00:04:59,923
But I also like onigiri with soft nori.

84
00:04:59,947 --> 00:05:02,630
It’s so good!

85
00:05:02,654 --> 00:05:05,945
There are so many kinds of onigiri.

86
00:05:05,968 --> 00:05:10,046
Are onigiri usually triangle-shaped?

87
00:05:10,069 --> 00:05:11,602
Yes, I do.

88
00:05:11,625 --> 00:05:15,676
The ones I make are triangular.

89
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:19,757
But there are round onigiri too.

90
00:05:19,780 --> 00:05:23,547
Round onigiri are cute, aren’t they?

91
00:05:23,570 --> 00:05:28,236
Do you put a lot of fillings inside your onigiri?

92
00:05:28,259 --> 00:05:31,859
No, not too much.

93
00:05:31,882 --> 00:05:34,694
Just a little bit.

94
00:05:34,718 --> 00:05:38,726
That way, you can really taste the rice.

95
00:05:38,749 --> 00:05:40,625
I see.

96
00:05:40,649 --> 00:05:44,249
The taste of the rice is important.

97
00:05:44,271 --> 00:05:47,679
Japanese rice is so delicious.

98
00:05:47,703 --> 00:05:49,574
That’s true.

99
00:05:49,597 --> 00:05:54,264
Onigiri is a wonderful part of Japanese cuisine.

100
00:05:54,287 --> 00:05:58,768
Do people around the world know about onigiri?

101
00:05:58,791 --> 00:06:00,325
Yes, I do.

102
00:06:00,348 --> 00:06:04,481
Many foreigners know about onigiri.

103
00:06:04,504 --> 00:06:07,241
They often see it in anime.

104
00:06:07,264 --> 00:06:11,331
Anime is amazing, isn’t it?

105
00:06:11,354 --> 00:06:14,720
Everyone loves onigiri!

106
00:06:14,743 --> 00:06:17,110
That’s wonderful to hear.

107
00:06:17,133 --> 00:06:21,570
Onigiri is so easy to make, too!

108
00:06:21,594 --> 00:06:24,448
Will my hands get messy?

109
00:06:24,471 --> 00:06:27,314
Let's use plastic wrap.

110
00:06:27,338 --> 00:06:29,871
Your hands won't get messy.

111
00:06:29,894 --> 00:06:32,527
It's so convenient!

112
00:06:32,550 --> 00:06:35,317
That's a great idea!

113
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:38,173
I'll try making it next time.

114
00:06:38,196 --> 00:06:41,196
You should definitely try it!

115
00:06:41,219 --> 00:06:44,219
You'll make delicious rice balls!

116
00:06:44,242 --> 00:06:48,778
Are warm rice balls tastier?

117
00:06:48,802 --> 00:06:52,212
Warm rice balls are delicious.

118
00:06:52,235 --> 00:06:56,501
But cold rice balls are tasty too!

119
00:06:56,524 --> 00:06:58,458
I see.

120
00:06:58,481 --> 00:07:02,014
Bento rice balls are usually cold, right?

121
00:07:02,037 --> 00:07:03,570
Yes, I do.

122
00:07:03,594 --> 00:07:07,605
Rice balls eaten outdoors are cold.

123
00:07:07,628 --> 00:07:12,497
But Japanese rice is delicious even when cold.

124
00:07:12,521 --> 00:07:16,121
That's why it's perfect for bentos!

125
00:07:16,144 --> 00:07:18,220
I see, that makes sense.

126
00:07:18,243 --> 00:07:23,810
Now, let's talk about making bentos in the morning.

127
00:07:23,833 --> 00:07:25,566
Sounds good!

128
00:07:25,589 --> 00:07:28,589
Let's dive into that topic.

129
00:07:28,613 --> 00:07:33,930
Let me know in the comments if you caught all that!

130
00:07:33,930 --> 00:07:35,430
Scene 3: Early Rising and Lunchbox Preparation

131
00:07:35,430 --> 00:07:39,281
Is making bentos in the morning tough?

132
00:07:39,305 --> 00:07:43,707
I don’t make them, so I’m not sure.

133
00:07:43,730 --> 00:07:47,307
What time do you wake up every morning?

134
00:07:47,331 --> 00:07:52,264
I wake up at 5 AM every day.

135
00:07:52,287 --> 00:07:54,221
5 AM?

136
00:07:54,244 --> 00:07:56,610
That’s really early!

137
00:07:56,633 --> 00:08:00,033
Yes, it is early.

138
00:08:00,056 --> 00:08:04,823
After waking up, I head straight to the kitchen.

139
00:08:04,846 --> 00:08:08,213
What do you do in the kitchen?

140
00:08:08,236 --> 00:08:12,469
First, I boil water.

141
00:08:12,492 --> 00:08:16,492
Then, I start preparing the bento.

142
00:08:16,515 --> 00:08:19,715
There’s no time in the morning, right?

143
00:08:19,738 --> 00:08:24,219
Nope, no time at all.

144
00:08:24,242 --> 00:08:27,739
So I make everything in a hurry.

145
00:08:27,762 --> 00:08:30,568
What kind of things do you make?

146
00:08:30,592 --> 00:08:33,883
I make simple side dishes.

147
00:08:33,907 --> 00:08:38,963
Like tamagoyaki or stir-fried veggies.

148
00:08:38,986 --> 00:08:41,360
Stir-fried veggies?

149
00:08:41,384 --> 00:08:43,184
Sounds good!

150
00:08:43,207 --> 00:08:47,340
Yeah, I chop the veggies.

151
00:08:47,363 --> 00:08:50,971
Then I stir-fry them in a pan.

152
00:08:50,995 --> 00:08:53,774
It’s done in just 5 minutes!

153
00:08:53,797 --> 00:08:55,730
5 minutes?

154
00:08:55,753 --> 00:08:58,123
That’s really early!

155
00:08:58,147 --> 00:09:03,180
Yep! Speed is key for morning cooking.

156
00:09:03,203 --> 00:09:05,936
What about tamagoyaki?

157
00:09:05,959 --> 00:09:09,174
Tamagoyaki is easy too!

158
00:09:09,197 --> 00:09:12,205
I use two eggs.

159
00:09:12,229 --> 00:09:15,629
It’s a little sweet.

160
00:09:15,652 --> 00:09:19,218
Sweet tamagoyaki? Sounds delicious!

161
00:09:19,241 --> 00:09:22,841
It is! So tasty.

162
00:09:22,864 --> 00:09:25,798
It goes perfectly with rice.

163
00:09:25,821 --> 00:09:29,421
How do I pack my bento box?

164
00:09:29,444 --> 00:09:32,645
Start by putting in the rice.

165
00:09:32,669 --> 00:09:36,202
Then add the side dishes.

166
00:09:36,225 --> 00:09:38,640
It looks so pretty!

167
00:09:38,664 --> 00:09:41,297
Is it difficult?

168
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:45,161
No, it’s not hard at all!

169
00:09:45,185 --> 00:09:49,785
I make it every day, so I’ve gotten really good at it.

170
00:09:49,808 --> 00:09:52,083
That’s wonderful!

171
00:09:52,107 --> 00:09:55,840
I wake up at 7 every morning.

172
00:09:55,863 --> 00:09:57,996
7 AM?

173
00:09:58,019 --> 00:10:01,996
There’s no time to make a bento at that hour!

174
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:04,462
No, there isn’t.

175
00:10:04,486 --> 00:10:07,953
I leave right after waking up.

176
00:10:07,975 --> 00:10:11,986
That’s why I end up going to the convenience store every day.

177
00:10:12,010 --> 00:10:14,024
That’s right.

178
00:10:14,047 --> 00:10:18,524
But waking up early in the morning is great, isn’t it?

179
00:10:18,548 --> 00:10:23,748
Yes, the morning air feels so refreshing.

180
00:10:23,771 --> 00:10:28,018
I want to start waking up at 6 AM from tomorrow!

181
00:10:28,042 --> 00:10:31,508
That’s great! Good luck!

182
00:10:31,531 --> 00:10:35,819
Do you ever struggle in the morning when you’re in a rush?

183
00:10:35,843 --> 00:10:39,320
Oh, all the time!

184
00:10:39,343 --> 00:10:43,522
Sometimes I forget really important things.

185
00:10:43,546 --> 00:10:46,984
You forget things? Like what?

186
00:10:47,007 --> 00:10:51,607
Alright, let’s talk about those tough days next.

187
00:10:51,630 --> 00:10:55,397
Sounds good. Let’s hear those stories!

188
00:10:55,420 --> 00:10:56,920
Scene 4: Stories of Troublesome Days

189
00:10:56,920 --> 00:11:01,453
Let’s talk about those days when everything goes wrong.

190
00:11:01,476 --> 00:11:03,757
Troublesome days?

191
00:11:03,781 --> 00:11:05,914
How's your day going?

192
00:11:05,937 --> 00:11:11,471
I forgot my chopsticks for my lunchbox yesterday.

193
00:11:11,494 --> 00:11:15,660
Wait, you forgot your chopsticks?

194
00:11:15,683 --> 00:11:18,457
That must have been rough.

195
00:11:18,481 --> 00:11:22,081
Yeah, I was really stuck.

196
00:11:22,104 --> 00:11:25,741
I realized it when it was time for lunch.

197
00:11:25,764 --> 00:11:27,898
What did you do?

198
00:11:27,921 --> 00:11:30,523
Did you borrow some from someone?

199
00:11:30,547 --> 00:11:34,947
Yeah, I borrowed chopsticks from a friend.

200
00:11:34,970 --> 00:11:37,987
So it all worked out.

201
00:11:38,011 --> 00:11:39,877
That’s a relief!

202
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:44,742
Last week, I bought a bento at a convenience store.

203
00:11:44,766 --> 00:11:48,382
Oh yeah? What did you get?

204
00:11:48,406 --> 00:11:51,504
I got some delicious pasta.

205
00:11:51,527 --> 00:11:55,586
But the store clerk didn’t give me a fork.

206
00:11:55,610 --> 00:12:00,176
Wait, no fork?

207
00:12:00,199 --> 00:12:05,670
Right. And I didn’t have a fork or chopsticks at the office.

208
00:12:05,694 --> 00:12:09,136
That must have been rough.

209
00:12:09,159 --> 00:12:11,093
What did you do?

210
00:12:11,116 --> 00:12:14,974
I went to a nearby 100-yen shop.

211
00:12:14,998 --> 00:12:17,864
I bought chopsticks there.

212
00:12:17,887 --> 00:12:20,302
A 100-yen shop, huh?

213
00:12:20,326 --> 00:12:23,326
Well, that worked out.

214
00:12:23,349 --> 00:12:28,915
Yeah, but then it was almost the end of my lunch break.

215
00:12:28,938 --> 00:12:31,505
I had to eat in a hurry.

216
00:12:31,528 --> 00:12:34,661
That sounds stressful!

217
00:12:34,684 --> 00:12:38,362
Have you had any other tough situations like that?

218
00:12:38,386 --> 00:12:45,119
I often shuffle my bento around inside the convenience store bag.

219
00:12:45,142 --> 00:12:48,275
The bento ends up tilted.

220
00:12:48,298 --> 00:12:52,899
Oh, so the bento gets tilted?

221
00:12:52,923 --> 00:12:58,498
Yeah, and the delicious juices spill out inside the bag.

222
00:12:58,521 --> 00:13:01,495
My bag gets all messy too.

223
00:13:01,519 --> 00:13:04,123
That sounds rough.

224
00:13:04,146 --> 00:13:08,279
The books in my bag get soaked too.

225
00:13:08,302 --> 00:13:12,072
Yeah, it’s really sad.

226
00:13:12,096 --> 00:13:16,355
That’s why lately, I’ve been walking super carefully.

227
00:13:16,379 --> 00:13:18,188
Sounds good!

228
00:13:18,212 --> 00:13:23,691
Bento is great, but sometimes it causes trouble, huh?

229
00:13:23,714 --> 00:13:25,281
That’s true.

230
00:13:25,304 --> 00:13:28,552
I’ll be more careful from now on.

231
00:13:28,575 --> 00:13:31,741
Yeah, let’s both be careful.

232
00:13:31,764 --> 00:13:36,764
Alright, next let’s talk about convenience store bento.

233
00:13:36,787 --> 00:13:38,521
Sounds good!

234
00:13:38,544 --> 00:13:41,226
Let's dive into that topic.

235
00:13:41,249 --> 00:13:42,749
Scene 5: Talking About Convenience Store Bento

236
00:13:42,749 --> 00:13:47,204
Let’s talk about convenience store bento today.

237
00:13:47,228 --> 00:13:48,917
Sounds good!

238
00:13:48,941 --> 00:13:53,959
I eat convenience store bento every day, you know.

239
00:13:53,982 --> 00:13:57,215
Which convenience store do you usually go to?

240
00:13:57,238 --> 00:14:01,038
I usually go to 7-Eleven.

241
00:14:01,061 --> 00:14:04,149
Is there one near you too?

242
00:14:04,173 --> 00:14:08,389
Yeah, there’s one near my place too.

243
00:14:08,412 --> 00:14:11,145
There’s a Lawson too.

244
00:14:11,168 --> 00:14:13,702
Lawson’s great too.

245
00:14:13,725 --> 00:14:17,493
Convenience stores have so many bento options.

246
00:14:17,517 --> 00:14:19,350
That’s true.

247
00:14:19,373 --> 00:14:23,574
What’s your favorite kind of bento?

248
00:14:23,597 --> 00:14:28,269
I love fried chicken bento the most.

249
00:14:28,293 --> 00:14:30,860
It’s so good!

250
00:14:30,882 --> 00:14:32,682
Fried chicken, huh?

251
00:14:32,705 --> 00:14:34,572
Sounds good!

252
00:14:34,595 --> 00:14:37,467
How much does it cost?

253
00:14:37,490 --> 00:14:40,757
Around 500 yen.

254
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:42,850
That’s really cheap!

255
00:14:42,874 --> 00:14:45,207
500 yen?

256
00:14:45,230 --> 00:14:47,563
That *is* cheap!

257
00:14:47,586 --> 00:14:51,153
Do they have hamburger steak bento too?

258
00:14:51,176 --> 00:14:53,393
Yeah, they do.

259
00:14:53,417 --> 00:14:57,029
The hamburger steak bento is delicious too.

260
00:14:57,052 --> 00:14:59,485
They have spaghetti too.

261
00:14:59,508 --> 00:15:03,075
There are so many varieties, huh?

262
00:15:03,098 --> 00:15:05,974
You never get tired of them, even if you eat them every day.

263
00:15:05,997 --> 00:15:08,443
Yeah, never.

264
00:15:08,467 --> 00:15:13,402
But I think homemade bento is a little better.

265
00:15:13,425 --> 00:15:15,558
Why’s that?

266
00:15:15,581 --> 00:15:19,421
Convenience store bento is super convenient, though.

267
00:15:19,444 --> 00:15:24,044
It is, but there’s not much veggies, you know?

268
00:15:24,067 --> 00:15:26,641
I’m a little worried about my health.

269
00:15:26,664 --> 00:15:28,722
Ah, I see.

270
00:15:28,746 --> 00:15:32,979
My homemade bento has lots of veggies.

271
00:15:33,002 --> 00:15:35,458
Sounds good!

272
00:15:35,482 --> 00:15:39,048
Convenience store bento has a lot of meat.

273
00:15:39,071 --> 00:15:41,505
Young people love that, though.

274
00:15:41,528 --> 00:15:43,328
That’s true.

275
00:15:43,351 --> 00:15:46,951
Do the staff heat it up for you at the store?

276
00:15:46,974 --> 00:15:48,440
Yes, I do.

277
00:15:48,463 --> 00:15:50,663
They ask, 'Would you like it heated up?'

278
00:15:50,686 --> 00:15:53,620
So I say, 'Yes, please.'

279
00:15:53,643 --> 00:15:57,109
A warm bento is just delicious.

280
00:15:57,132 --> 00:15:58,905
That’s true.

281
00:15:58,929 --> 00:16:02,529
Warm rice is the best, isn’t it?

282
00:16:02,552 --> 00:16:04,241
Yes, I do.

283
00:16:04,265 --> 00:16:08,598
That’s why I love convenience store bentos!

284
00:16:08,621 --> 00:16:12,788
Did you know? Japanese convenience stores exist overseas too.

285
00:16:12,811 --> 00:16:14,484
Have you heard about that?

286
00:16:14,507 --> 00:16:17,116
Yes, I have!

287
00:16:17,140 --> 00:16:21,599
But the bento options are different, right?

288
00:16:21,622 --> 00:16:23,875
Why do you think that is?

289
00:16:23,899 --> 00:16:26,065
I’m curious!

290
00:16:26,088 --> 00:16:30,530
Because they feature the country’s famous local foods.

291
00:16:30,554 --> 00:16:32,688
That sounds so interesting!

292
00:16:32,711 --> 00:16:36,544
Wow, that *is* interesting!

293
00:16:36,567 --> 00:16:40,808
I’d love to visit a foreign convenience store someday.

294
00:16:40,832 --> 00:16:42,565
Sounds good!

295
00:16:42,588 --> 00:16:48,200
Japanese convenience store bentos are actually popular worldwide, you know!

296
00:16:48,223 --> 00:16:49,990
That’s so great to hear!

297
00:16:50,013 --> 00:16:55,246
Homemade meals are wonderful, but convenience stores are amazing too!

298
00:16:55,269 --> 00:16:56,636
Yes, I do.

299
00:16:56,659 --> 00:17:01,426
Alright, let’s talk about our favorite side dishes next!

300
00:17:01,449 --> 00:17:03,226
Sounds good!

301
00:17:03,250 --> 00:17:05,983
Let's dive into that topic.

302
00:17:06,006 --> 00:17:07,506
Scene 6: How to Use Japanese Particles

303
00:17:07,506 --> 00:17:09,006
Scene 7: All About Bento Boxes

304
00:17:09,006 --> 00:17:14,006
Today, let’s chat about bento boxes!

305
00:17:14,029 --> 00:17:16,700
Bento boxes?

306
00:17:16,723 --> 00:17:18,690
Sounds good!

307
00:17:18,713 --> 00:17:23,786
Your bento box is so cute!

308
00:17:23,809 --> 00:17:26,069
Thank you!

309
00:17:26,093 --> 00:17:29,938
This is a blue bento box.

310
00:17:29,962 --> 00:17:33,035
Where did you buy it?

311
00:17:33,058 --> 00:17:35,029
Was it at a department store?

312
00:17:35,053 --> 00:17:38,586
No, not a department store.

313
00:17:38,609 --> 00:17:41,810
I got it at a 100-yen shop!

314
00:17:41,834 --> 00:17:44,889
A 100-yen shop?

315
00:17:44,912 --> 00:17:47,556
That’s really cheap!

316
00:17:47,580 --> 00:17:50,613
Yep, it was just 100 yen!

317
00:17:50,636 --> 00:17:54,669
But it’s super convenient.

318
00:17:54,692 --> 00:17:57,382
What makes it so convenient?

319
00:17:57,406 --> 00:18:01,085
First, it’s really lightweight.

320
00:18:01,109 --> 00:18:05,164
I carry it in my bag every day.

321
00:18:05,187 --> 00:18:09,636
Since it’s not heavy, it’s perfect for me!

322
00:18:09,659 --> 00:18:12,593
Lightweight is definitely a plus!

323
00:18:12,616 --> 00:18:15,449
Is it big in size?

324
00:18:15,472 --> 00:18:19,566
No, it’s not too big.

325
00:18:19,589 --> 00:18:23,556
It’s just the right size for me.

326
00:18:23,579 --> 00:18:27,155
Does the lid close tightly?

327
00:18:27,179 --> 00:18:30,712
Yes, it seals tightly!

328
00:18:30,735 --> 00:18:34,602
So my side dishes never spill out.

329
00:18:34,625 --> 00:18:37,392
That’s reassuring!

330
00:18:37,415 --> 00:18:44,270
You know, 100-yen shops have all kinds of bento boxes.

331
00:18:44,294 --> 00:18:49,061
Do they have round or square ones?

332
00:18:49,084 --> 00:18:52,550
Yes, they have tons!

333
00:18:52,573 --> 00:18:56,869
There are even red and black ones too.

334
00:18:56,893 --> 00:18:59,226
Black ones?

335
00:18:59,249 --> 00:19:02,049
Those would suit guys well, wouldn’t they?

336
00:19:02,072 --> 00:19:06,906
Yeah, guys use them a lot too!

337
00:19:06,929 --> 00:19:12,783
I don’t cook, but I want a bento box.

338
00:19:12,806 --> 00:19:16,239
Why do you want a bento box if you don’t cook?

339
00:19:16,262 --> 00:19:19,068
You don’t cook, huh?

340
00:19:19,092 --> 00:19:22,759
I’ll use it for small things.

341
00:19:22,782 --> 00:19:26,651
It’ll keep my work desk nice and tidy.

342
00:19:26,675 --> 00:19:29,851
Oh, that’s a great idea!

343
00:19:29,874 --> 00:19:34,509
I’ll put pens and medicine in the box.

344
00:19:34,533 --> 00:19:39,566
Yeah. And if it’s cute, I’ll just leave it on my desk.

345
00:19:39,589 --> 00:19:41,856
That’s really nice.

346
00:19:41,879 --> 00:19:44,974
Let’s go to the 100-yen shop!

347
00:19:44,997 --> 00:19:49,931
Looking at all the different boxes is so much fun!

348
00:19:49,954 --> 00:19:55,730
Yeah, I’ll stop by the store near my place on the way home today.

349
00:19:55,753 --> 00:19:58,388
They have some great boxes there!

350
00:19:58,411 --> 00:20:01,345
The ones for bento are nice too.

351
00:20:01,368 --> 00:20:06,334
Yeah. I’ll use it when I make bento someday.

352
00:20:06,357 --> 00:20:08,291
Sounds good!

353
00:20:08,314 --> 00:20:13,080
Homemade bento is so delicious.

354
00:20:13,103 --> 00:20:19,375
Alright, next let’s talk about bento and iced tea.

355
00:20:19,399 --> 00:20:23,199
Yeah, let’s talk about that!

356
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:24,722
Scene 8: Bento and Iced Green Tea

357
00:20:24,722 --> 00:20:30,289
Today, let’s talk about bento and iced tea.

358
00:20:30,312 --> 00:20:32,086
Sounds good!

359
00:20:32,109 --> 00:20:37,976
Whenever I eat bento, I always drink tea with it.

360
00:20:37,999 --> 00:20:39,999
What kind of tea?

361
00:20:40,022 --> 00:20:42,155
Green tea?

362
00:20:42,178 --> 00:20:44,032
Oolong tea?

363
00:20:44,056 --> 00:20:48,143
I love green tea.

364
00:20:48,166 --> 00:20:52,166
Iced green tea is so refreshing!

365
00:20:52,189 --> 00:20:55,224
I like green tea too.

366
00:20:55,247 --> 00:20:59,414
But I make my own tea at home.

367
00:20:59,437 --> 00:21:02,575
You make it at home?

368
00:21:02,599 --> 00:21:04,466
Wow, that’s impressive!

369
00:21:04,489 --> 00:21:07,824
Yeah, it’s super easy.

370
00:21:07,847 --> 00:21:12,065
Just put tea leaves and water in a bottle.

371
00:21:12,088 --> 00:21:14,521
Then put it in the fridge.

372
00:21:14,544 --> 00:21:16,711
That’s it?

373
00:21:16,734 --> 00:21:19,610
Wow, that *is* easy!

374
00:21:19,633 --> 00:21:22,437
Yep, it’s really simple.

375
00:21:22,460 --> 00:21:28,238
Then I just pour it into my bottle and bring it to work every day.

376
00:21:28,261 --> 00:21:31,672
That bottle is so cute!

377
00:21:31,696 --> 00:21:34,630
Where did you buy it?

378
00:21:34,653 --> 00:21:38,286
I bought it at a department store.

379
00:21:38,309 --> 00:21:42,578
It was a little expensive, but I love it.

380
00:21:42,601 --> 00:21:44,935
That’s a great bottle.

381
00:21:44,957 --> 00:21:48,014
Does it keep drinks hot too?

382
00:21:48,037 --> 00:21:50,906
Yeah, it does.

383
00:21:50,930 --> 00:21:55,707
In winter, I use it for hot tea or black tea.

384
00:21:55,730 --> 00:21:59,064
You use it all year round!

385
00:21:59,087 --> 00:22:01,253
It’s so convenient.

386
00:22:01,276 --> 00:22:04,370
Yeah, I use it every day.

387
00:22:04,394 --> 00:22:09,561
I don’t buy tea at convenience stores, so it saves me money.

388
00:22:09,584 --> 00:22:12,655
That’s really smart!

389
00:22:12,678 --> 00:22:17,078
I buy tea at the convenience store every day.

390
00:22:17,101 --> 00:22:19,434
How much is one bottle?

391
00:22:19,457 --> 00:22:22,824
It's about 150 yen.

392
00:22:22,847 --> 00:22:25,314
150 yen?

393
00:22:25,337 --> 00:22:30,903
If you buy it every day, that adds up to a lot of money in a month.

394
00:22:30,926 --> 00:22:35,660
Yes, it comes to over 3,000 yen.

395
00:22:35,683 --> 00:22:38,649
That's really expensive.

396
00:22:38,672 --> 00:22:41,122
It sure is.

397
00:22:41,146 --> 00:22:45,440
Using a reusable bottle makes it much cheaper.

398
00:22:45,463 --> 00:22:47,511
That’s true.

399
00:22:47,534 --> 00:22:51,073
I want a reusable bottle too.

400
00:22:51,097 --> 00:22:53,230
You should definitely get one.

401
00:22:53,253 --> 00:22:56,267
There are so many different designs.

402
00:22:56,291 --> 00:22:57,824
Yes, I do.

403
00:22:57,847 --> 00:23:00,937
Besides tea, what else do you put in it?

404
00:23:00,961 --> 00:23:04,620
Sometimes I put water in it.

405
00:23:04,643 --> 00:23:09,177
Hot water is good for your health too.

406
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:10,766
Hot water?

407
00:23:10,789 --> 00:23:15,838
Yes, drinking it in the morning warms you up.

408
00:23:15,862 --> 00:23:17,720
I see.

409
00:23:17,744 --> 00:23:21,826
I drink cold water in the morning.

410
00:23:21,849 --> 00:23:24,849
Cold water is refreshing too.

411
00:23:24,872 --> 00:23:29,490
But tea goes really well with a bento.

412
00:23:29,513 --> 00:23:33,049
Yes, I think so too.

413
00:23:33,073 --> 00:23:36,850
I'll drink lots of tea starting tomorrow.

414
00:23:36,874 --> 00:23:41,874
Now, let's talk about how to spend your lunch break.

415
00:23:41,897 --> 00:23:43,397
Scene 9: How to Spend Your Lunch Break

416
00:23:43,397 --> 00:23:48,882
Today, let's talk about how to spend your lunch break.

417
00:23:48,905 --> 00:23:50,960
Sounds good!

418
00:23:50,983 --> 00:23:56,150
Our company's lunch break is one hour, right?

419
00:23:56,173 --> 00:24:01,106
Yes, from 12 to 1 PM.

420
00:24:01,129 --> 00:24:06,027
Where do you usually eat your bento?

421
00:24:06,051 --> 00:24:11,658
I always eat in this break room.

422
00:24:11,681 --> 00:24:15,329
It's so quiet here.

423
00:24:15,352 --> 00:24:20,442
Yes, it's quiet and very clean.

424
00:24:20,465 --> 00:24:24,313
You can also see the view outside well.

425
00:24:24,337 --> 00:24:26,306
That’s true.

426
00:24:26,330 --> 00:24:32,130
You can see the blue sky and green trees from the window.

427
00:24:32,153 --> 00:24:36,166
Yes, it feels really good.

428
00:24:36,189 --> 00:24:38,661
It's relaxing.

429
00:24:38,685 --> 00:24:42,752
What do you do after you finish eating?

430
00:24:42,775 --> 00:24:46,411
I read a book.

431
00:24:46,434 --> 00:24:51,300
Then I listen to some music.

432
00:24:51,323 --> 00:24:53,523
Sounds good!

433
00:24:53,546 --> 00:24:56,553
What kind of books do you read?

434
00:24:56,576 --> 00:24:59,843
I read novels.

435
00:24:59,867 --> 00:25:02,867
They're really interesting.

436
00:25:02,890 --> 00:25:06,623
What kind of music do you listen to?

437
00:25:06,646 --> 00:25:09,819
I listen to calm music.

438
00:25:09,843 --> 00:25:13,450
Sometimes I take a short nap.

439
00:25:13,473 --> 00:25:16,772
You nap in the break room?

440
00:25:16,796 --> 00:25:20,068
Yes, just for 10 minutes.

441
00:25:20,092 --> 00:25:26,178
It helps me work hard again in the afternoon.

442
00:25:26,202 --> 00:25:28,276
That's a great idea!

443
00:25:28,299 --> 00:25:32,780
I go outside during my lunch break.

444
00:25:32,804 --> 00:25:36,171
What do you do outside?

445
00:25:36,193 --> 00:25:39,793
I walk in the nearby park.

446
00:25:39,816 --> 00:25:43,307
Then I go to the convenience store.

447
00:25:43,331 --> 00:25:46,798
Walking is good for your health.

448
00:25:46,821 --> 00:25:49,917
Yes, it does count as exercise.

449
00:25:49,940 --> 00:25:54,038
But I don’t go outside on rainy days.

450
00:25:54,062 --> 00:25:58,151
What do you do on rainy days?

451
00:25:58,174 --> 00:26:02,508
On rainy days, I eat bread here.

452
00:26:02,531 --> 00:26:06,664
Then, I watch videos on my phone.

453
00:26:06,687 --> 00:26:08,454
Videos?

454
00:26:08,477 --> 00:26:11,243
What kind of videos?

455
00:26:11,266 --> 00:26:16,033
I watch travel vlogs and cooking videos.

456
00:26:16,056 --> 00:26:18,423
That sounds fun!

457
00:26:18,446 --> 00:26:21,579
Is an hour too long?

458
00:26:21,602 --> 00:26:23,469
Or is it too short?

459
00:26:23,492 --> 00:26:26,626
I think it’s too short.

460
00:26:26,649 --> 00:26:30,108
I wish we had more break time.

461
00:26:30,131 --> 00:26:32,939
I think it’s too short too.

462
00:26:32,962 --> 00:26:37,851
But this one hour is really important.

463
00:26:37,874 --> 00:26:39,607
That’s true.

464
00:26:39,630 --> 00:26:44,323
Let’s enjoy a delicious bento and take a good rest.

465
00:26:44,347 --> 00:26:47,414
Yes, let’s do that.

466
00:26:47,437 --> 00:26:51,109
Now, let’s talk about our final topic.

467
00:26:51,132 --> 00:26:52,632
Scene 10: All About Bento – The Art of Japanese Lunchboxes

468
00:26:52,632 --> 00:26:56,432
Let’s wrap up today with our final discussion.

469
00:26:56,455 --> 00:26:59,288
The theme is: 'Let’s eat here again tomorrow.'

470
00:26:59,311 --> 00:27:01,344
That’s our topic for today.

471
00:27:01,367 --> 00:27:03,178
Sounds good!

472
00:27:03,202 --> 00:27:07,891
We’ve talked a lot about bento up until now, haven’t we?

473
00:27:07,914 --> 00:27:09,181
Yes, I do.

474
00:27:09,205 --> 00:27:18,476
We’ve covered what goes inside, convenience store bento, bento boxes, tea—so many things!

475
00:27:18,499 --> 00:27:21,299
It’s been so much fun.

476
00:27:21,322 --> 00:27:26,088
I’ve grown to love bento even more.

477
00:27:26,111 --> 00:27:29,586
That makes me really happy to hear.

478
00:27:29,610 --> 00:27:34,343
Bento is a wonderful part of Japanese culture.

479
00:27:34,366 --> 00:27:35,733
Yes, I do.

480
00:27:35,756 --> 00:27:39,089
It’s not just a meal, after all.

481
00:27:39,112 --> 00:27:40,687
That’s right.

482
00:27:40,710 --> 00:27:47,243
A bento carries the care and kindness of the person who made it.

483
00:27:47,266 --> 00:27:48,900
Yes, I do.

484
00:27:48,923 --> 00:27:56,328
Convenience store bento are tasty and handy, but homemade ones feel even warmer.

485
00:27:56,351 --> 00:27:58,085
That’s true.

486
00:27:58,108 --> 00:28:03,508
The time spent eating a bento is such a happy moment.

487
00:28:03,531 --> 00:28:04,664
Yes, I do.

488
00:28:04,687 --> 00:28:07,454
I think so too.

489
00:28:07,477 --> 00:28:12,319
Eating a bento always gives me energy.

490
00:28:12,342 --> 00:28:14,120
Sounds good!

491
00:28:14,144 --> 00:28:19,114
I want to make my own delicious bento someday.

492
00:28:19,137 --> 00:28:21,537
You should definitely try it!

493
00:28:21,560 --> 00:28:26,832
Let’s start with something simple, like rice balls and tamagoyaki.

494
00:28:26,856 --> 00:28:28,223
Okay!

495
00:28:28,246 --> 00:28:30,729
I’ll do my best!

496
00:28:30,752 --> 00:28:33,785
I’ll show you when I do!

497
00:28:33,808 --> 00:28:36,142
I can’t wait to see it!

498
00:28:36,165 --> 00:28:39,340
I’m sure it’ll be a beautiful bento!

499
00:28:39,363 --> 00:28:40,596
Yes, I do.

500
00:28:40,619 --> 00:28:42,997
I’m really looking forward to it!

501
00:28:43,021 --> 00:28:47,428
I’ll make and bring a bento again tomorrow.

502
00:28:47,452 --> 00:28:49,252
Sounds good!

503
00:28:49,275 --> 00:28:52,108
What’s in tomorrow’s bento?

504
00:28:52,131 --> 00:28:56,181
Tomorrow, I’ll pack some delicious hamburger steak.

505
00:28:56,205 --> 00:28:58,338
Hamburger steak?

506
00:28:58,361 --> 00:29:01,413
That sounds amazing!

507
00:29:01,436 --> 00:29:03,118
Yes, I do.

508
00:29:03,142 --> 00:29:06,008
It’s one of my specialties.

509
00:29:06,031 --> 00:29:07,600
Sounds good!

510
00:29:07,624 --> 00:29:10,791
I’ll head to the convenience store tomorrow.

511
00:29:10,814 --> 00:29:14,507
I’ll buy my favorite fried chicken bento.

512
00:29:14,530 --> 00:29:16,863
Fried chicken sounds great too.

513
00:29:16,886 --> 00:29:21,053
Let’s grab lunch here together during our break.

514
00:29:21,076 --> 00:29:22,442
Yes, I do.

515
00:29:22,465 --> 00:29:24,665
Let’s eat together.

516
00:29:24,688 --> 00:29:27,505
I’ll meet you here at noon.

517
00:29:27,528 --> 00:29:28,862
Yes, I do.

518
00:29:28,885 --> 00:29:30,485
Got it.

519
00:29:30,508 --> 00:29:35,241
Let’s enjoy a good meal and power through the afternoon work.

520
00:29:35,264 --> 00:29:36,664
Yes, I do.

521
00:29:36,687 --> 00:29:38,941
I’ll bring tea too.

522
00:29:38,964 --> 00:29:40,823
Thank you!

523
00:29:40,847 --> 00:29:43,613
See you tomorrow, then.

524
00:29:43,636 --> 00:29:44,770
Yes, I do.

525
00:29:44,793 --> 00:29:46,526
See you tomorrow.